# bug-01-heap-overflow.keys -- demonstrates isocline-issues.rst #1
# (critical): sbuf_strdup_from_utf8() in src/stringbuf.c allocates
# exactly len bytes and then writes a terminating NUL at s[len], one
# byte past the allocation, whenever every input character is a
# single byte. This is reachable on every ic_readline() call when the
# terminal is not UTF-8 -- hit here by running under LC_ALL=en_US.US-ASCII
# (see the ENV_bug-01-heap-overflow override in the Makefile; tty.c
# treats the "C" locale itself as UTF-8-capable, so plain "C" will not
# reach this path).
#
# Typing plain ASCII and pressing ENTER is enough to trigger the
# overflow; under the ASan build the jig uses by default, this should
# show up as a heap-buffer-overflow report in the captured output.
# Once issue #1 is fixed, this report will disappear and the test
# becomes a plain regression guard -- re-accept the golden output at
# that point.
i 2
+ hello
k ENTER
w 50
q
